      "descent_note": null,
      "explicit_ages": [],
      "identity_note": "Literary figure: Judith makes Nebuchadnezzar king of Assyria at Nineveh, after the return from exile (4:3, 5:19), and demands worship as a god (3:8, 6:2). This combination fits no historical reign (the Babylonian Nebuchadnezzar II never ruled from Nineveh, which had fallen in 612 BC, and he predates the return). Kept as a separate person rather than mapped to the existing nebuchadnezzar id so that the book's fictional dates (years 12-18) are not attached to Nebuchadnezzar II."
    },
