  "notes": "Text read in full (339 verses). Judith's genealogy (8:1) is recorded as a parent chain Merari<-Ox<-Joseph<-Oziel<-Elkiah<-Ananias<-Gideon<-Raphaim<-Ahitub<-Elihu<-Eliab<-Nathanael<-Salamiel(shelumiel)<-Salasadai(zurishaddai); \"son of Israel\" treated as distant descent from Jacob. The book's Nebuchadnezzar (\"king of the Assyrians in Nineveh\") is kept as a separate literary figure (nebuchadnezzar-judith), as are Arphaxad and Joakim. Ozias/Chabris/Charmis are Bethulia's rulers with stated fathers (6:15). The anonymous \"king of Egypt\" of 5:11 is mapped to pharaoh-exodus. Unnamed but skipped as non-unique/groups: Holofernes' servants and guards, the hundred escorts, the elders. Holofernes refs include named verses plus key descriptive references."
